# STYLESHEETS ARE LF, ALWAYS -- BECAUSE A WINDOWS EDIT OTHERWISE REWRITES THE WHOLE FILE.
#
# Measured on PR #1808: a two-rule change to field-ops-app-vite/src/index.css arrived as
# +8,480 / -8,400 -- every line in the file replaced. Nothing had been reformatted. The
# working copy is materialised CRLF on Windows (core.autocrlf=true), an edit round-tripped
# the file, and the CRLF bytes reached the commit instead of being normalised on the way in.
# The real change was 84 lines; `--ignore-space-at-eol` was the only thing that could see it.
#
# A diff nobody can read is a diff nobody reviews, and this is the largest file in the client.
# Pinning it removes the possibility rather than relying on the next person to notice.
#
# THIS ADDS NO CHURN. The one tracked stylesheet is already stored LF
# (`git ls-files --eol` reports i/lf), so the rule states what the repository already holds.
*.css text eol=lf
